                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238645209",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198169085960",
                            "num_reviews": 27,
                            "playtime_forever": 435,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 427,
                            "playtime_at_review": 435,
                            "deck_playtime_at_review": 8,
                            "last_played": 1793055825
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I recommend this game but only if you like very simple games and you like the looks of the Store Page. There is NO story in this game. You essentially have two choices to start and then you unlock a third. You have to beat the game with all three choices to get all the stars to finish the last Achievement. Each choice has only one map and each point on the map has Easy, Medium, and Hard (each gives one Star). I you win the point on Hard you get all three Stars. The Achievements are very straight forward.\r\n\r\nThe game is pretty easy if you don't mind grinding. You can do Easy or Medium as many times as you want and you get a ridiculous amount of XP each win. You can easily level up to 22 (the cap) before you finish all the Hard options on the map. As I said, there is zero story. You just fight combats. It is very simple and straight forward.\r\n\r\nThe option you unlock took me a bit to figure out since the level cap didn't reset when I started the map. I think I figured out that you increase you ability to summon units by collecting the blue and red crystals on the map. At least I think that is what's happening.\r\n\r\nI played the sequel (Necromancer's Return) which was originally Beasts Battle 2. That game has many improvements over this one and it takes a bit longer to complete. I liked that the sequel lets you see how many of a particular unit you have lost so you know if you need to resurrect any of the unit.\r\n\r\nI won't play this game again but I don't regret playing through once and I usually wait until games are significantly discounted so I think this was worth the price on sale. There isn't much strategy but it is fun enough to pass a few hours.",
